{
  "_comment": [
    "Benchmark ideas for retrieval evaluation.",
    "",
    "`intent` is populated by `--refresh-intents` (one real LLM call per case) and",
    "then reused. Caching it is deliberate: if intent parsing varied between the",
    "baseline run and the after run, the two would not be comparable and any",
    "measured change could just be the LLM phrasing things differently.",
    "",
    "`known_competitors` is hand-authored. It is the only relevance signal here",
    "with a human ground truth, which is why it exists despite being narrow.",
    "Names should be distinctive enough to match on (avoid generic words).",
    "INTENTS BELOW ARE HAND-AUTHORED, not produced by the real IntentParser: the configured LLM gateway returns 401 (token unusable), so --refresh-intents cannot run. They follow the rules in llm/prompts/intent_parser.txt (3-6 concrete searchable nouns; Chinese keywords only for Chinese input). Re-run --refresh-intents once a working key exists, and re-baseline if they change."
  ],
